  "summary": "Current REQ-001 is substantial, scope-aligned, and no longer looks superficial. It delivers real canonical schema, enums, constraints, PostgreSQL triggers, Alembic migration logic, and non-trivial PostgreSQL-backed tests. It is ready for later evaluation. It is not yet a strong promotion candidate because promotion-facing evidence is still weaker than the docs imply: downgrade coverage does not prove seeded-data reversibility, and the aws/onprem runtime guidance is mostly documentary rather than executable evidence.",
